    "title": "China's Actions 'Conflict Directly' With IMF's Core Mission: Economist",
    "text": "China still enjoys the status of a country with an emerging economy at the U.N., despite being one of the world leaders. Why is the International Monetary Fund seemingly skewed in its favor and how is China taking advantage? Daniel Lacalle, chief economist at Tressis hedge fund and author of \"Freedom or Equality,\" joins us to discuss.\nChina's Actions 'Conflict Directly' With IMF's Core Mission: Economist\nDaniel Lacalle, economist, discussed US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent calling on the IMF and the World Bank to take a tougher stance on China.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 10/22/2025, 11:59:17 PM EDT",
